Implement user story SKY-004-be-2: Test Express REST API server with vitest + supertest — Tests

## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts using vitest + supertest with at least 8 tests covering all server route scenarios: /health (with and without RAPIDAPI_KEY), / (static file serving), /search (valid params, missing params, adults default, adults non-numeric), /cheapest (valid, empty results, missing params), RAPIDAPI_KEY absent (503 gating), and SkyscannerClient error handling (500). SkyscannerClient must be mocked via vi.mock so no real HTTP calls occur. Depends on SKY-004-be-1 (server implementation must exist).

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.test.ts uses vitest + supertest; SkyscannerClient is mocked via vi.mock (or equivalent) so no real HTTP calls are made during `vitest run`
- Test: GET /health returns 200 with { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- Test: GET / returns 200 text/html with body matching the contents of src/public/index.html (read from file, not hardcoded)
- Test: GET /search with valid params returns 200 { flights, count, searchedAt } where count === flights.length; missing required param → 400; adults absent → default 1; adults non-numeric → 400
- Test: GET /cheapest with valid params returns 200 with cheapest FlightResult; empty results → 404; missing required param → 400
- Test: RAPIDAPI_KEY absent → /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; /health and / return their normal responses
- Test: SkyscannerClient throws error → server returns 500 { error } without crash or unhandled promise rejection
- `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0 with no type errors; `vitest run` exits 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } — uptime is process.uptime()
- GET /health is NOT gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY — it works regardless of environment variable presence
- GET / returns 200 with Content-Type text/html — body is contents of src/public/index.html read at runtime via fs.readFileSync
- GET / is NOT gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET / returns 500 { error: 'Failed to load dashboard' } if index.html cannot be read
- GET /search requires RAPIDAPI_KEY — returns 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } if env var absent
- GET /cheapest requires RAPIDAPI_KEY — returns 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } if env var absent
- Query params for /search and /cheapest are: from, to, date (all required), adults (optional)
- Missing required params (from, to, or date) returns 400 { error: 'Missing required parameter(s): from, to, date' }
- adults defaults to 1 when absent
- adults non-numeric or non-integer returns 400 { error: 'Invalid adults: must be an integer' }
- adults=0 is VALID — no lower-bound check exists in source
- adults negative values are VALID — no lower-bound check exists in source
- GET /search returns 200 { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: string } where count === flights.length
- searchedAt is new Date().toISOString() — ISO 8601 timestamp
- GET /cheapest returns 200 with single FlightResult object (the one with lowest price)
- GET /cheapest returns 404 { error: 'No flights found' } when flights array is empty
- SkyscannerClient constructor throws if no apiKey provided and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent: error message is 'Missing RapidAPI key: provide 'apiKey' to SkyscannerClient or set RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable'
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights returns FlightResult[] with fields: price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- Server catches SkyscannerClient errors and returns 500 { error: 'Failed to fetch flights from upstream' } without crashing
- Server uses require.main === module guard — listen() only called when file is entrypoint
- app is exported separately from listen() for test imports
- PUBLIC_INDEX_HTML_PATH is path.resolve(__dirname, 'public', 'index.html')

## Mock Strategy
Mock SkyscannerClient via vi.mock('./skyscanner/client', () => ({ SkyscannerClient: vi.fn() })) with vi.hoisted to define mock class before module load; use vi.stubEnv to control RAPIDAPI_KEY; use beforeEach(() => vi.clearAllMocks()) to reset between tests

